WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.770
Every rainy season, the road to Musa's

2
00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.670
school floods at the low bridge.

3
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:08.170
Last year a minibus drove

4
00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.250
in and got stuck.

5
00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:12.850
Nobody was hurt, but nobody had

6
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:14.990
known how deep the water was.

7
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.460
Today: turn a problem in your

8
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.860
community into a connected design.

9
00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:25.050
Good projects start with a problem and the

10
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.350
people who have it, not with a gadget.

11
00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:29.610
Ask them what goes wrong,

12
00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.670
when, and who gets hurt.

13
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.200
Then write what success looks like:

14
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.720
nobody drives into deep water again.

15
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.690
Every connected design has four parts.

16
00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.400
Sense: a sensor measures

17
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.380
the water's depth.

18
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.100
Decide: a small computer

19
00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.540
checks if it's too deep.

20
00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.120
Act: a warning light flashes.

21
00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:54.430
Connect: a message warns

22
00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:56.090
drivers before they set off.

23
00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.130
There's always more than one design.

24
00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.920
First, a flashing light at the

25
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.300
bridge, with no network.

26
00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.140
Second, the light plus text

27
00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.500
alerts to drivers' phones.

28
00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.510
Third, a camera streaming live

29
00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:12.190
video of the bridge to an app.

30
00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.920
Weigh every design on the same things.

31
00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:19.950
Cost: can people afford it, and fix it?

32
00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.770
Power: will it last a cloudy week?

33
00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.780
Safety: what happens when it fails?

34
00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:28.470
Privacy: does it watch

35
00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:30.030
people who never agreed?

36
00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:31.680
Quick check!

37
00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.160
The water sensor at the bridge

38
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.240
breaks during a storm.

39
00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:37.640
What should the warning light do?

40
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:40.560
Flash, and report it.

41
00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:44.040
A dark light tells drivers it's safe:

42
00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.560
the most dangerous message of all.

43
00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:49.350
Good designs fail safe: when

44
00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:51.050
they can't tell, they warn.

45
00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:56.240
Now score each design from one to five on

46
00:01:56.240 --> 00:01:58.860
each thing, and agree with the people

47
00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:01.060
affected how much each matters.

48
00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.730
Here, safety counts most.

49
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.620
The light with text alerts wins:

50
00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.080
cheap, low power, early warnings,

51
00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.760
and it films nobody.

52
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:16.390
Last, present your design so others can

53
00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:19.390
judge and improve it: the problem, your

54
00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:22.210
drawing, your scores, and what could go

55
00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:22.450
wrong.

56
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.480
Then ask the people it's

57
00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.060
for: what did we miss?

58
00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:27.860
Your turn.

59
00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:32.010
Grace's design scores best, but she never

60
00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.330
asked the minibus drivers about it.

61
00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:37.070
What should she do before building it?

62
00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.760
Ask the drivers first: the people it's

63
00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.200
for know what your scores miss.

64
00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:45.400
Remember: start from a real problem,

65
00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:49.200
then sense, decide, act and connect.

66
00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:51.770
Weigh designs on cost,

67
00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.350
power, safety and privacy.

68
00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.350
Then share it, and improve it.

69
00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:00.410
Try it this week: pick a problem

70
00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:03.110
near you, like a tank that runs

71
00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:05.030
dry or a hot classroom.

72
00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:08.330
Draw your design as four boxes:

73
00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:12.630
sense, decide, act, connect.

74
00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.900
Score two designs, then ask

75
00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.580
someone at home what you missed.
